# XBD 4.5 Directory Protection
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The restricted deletion bit exists only under the XSI option (S_ISVTX in
# <sys/stat.h>), so the assertions are conditional. The refusals are tested
# by XSH.unlink.018, XSH.rmdir.012, XSH.rename.028 and .029, and the owner
# of the file by XSH.unlink.020, XSH.rmdir.013 and XSH.rename.030; these
# assertions add the owner of the directory and the privileged process.
# Whether a file the process can write may also be removed is
# implementation-defined and is avoided: the entries here are never
# writable by the process.

assertion  XBD.4.5-directory-protection.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.5
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       In a directory with S_ISVTX set that a process owns and can
           write, a process without privileges, that is not the owner of
           the entries and cannot write them (mode 0644 files and a mode
           0755 directory owned by another user), can unlink() a file,
           rename() a file within the directory, and rmdir() the empty
           directory.
note       Gated on XSI: section 4.5 is not shaded but the bit it governs is XSI (Q-214).
needs      root
test       t/001-dir-owner.c

assertion  XBD.4.5-directory-protection.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.5
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       In a directory with S_ISVTX set, owned by one user and writable
           by all, a process with appropriate privileges can unlink() and
           rename() files and rmdir() a directory that belong to another
           user.
note       Gated on XSI: section 4.5 is not shaded but the bit it governs is XSI (Q-214).
needs      root
test       t/002-privileged.c
